        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Dashboard: widget write-back — persist widget state via a setState bridge capability",
        "body": "> 📦 **Part of the modular-dashboard package** — master hub **#101136** (architecture diagrams · bottom-up merge order · the full per-PR test map).\n>\n> 🧪 **Try this PR:** approve a stateful custom widget (e.g. the `notes` starter), type, and reload → state persists via the jailed `setState`; a stale `expectedVersion` write is rejected.\n\n---\n\n> Give sandboxed widgets memory: a jailed, approval-gated `setState` capability that turns custom widgets from views into stateful apps.\n\nCloses #101137. **Stacked on #101098** (the sandboxed custom-widget host) — that PR lands first; this targets `main` with a cumulative diff, so review the new `state`-related files as the delta.\n\n## What problem this solves\nCustom widgets today are read-only: the postMessage bridge lets a widget *ask* the parent for data, but there's no way to *save* anything — so an agent-built notes pad, kanban, or game resets on every reload. This adds the one missing primitive: per-widget, jailed, size-capped state, without loosening the sandbox.\n\n## What's in this PR\n- New gateway RPCs `dashboard.widget.state.get` / `.set` (read/write scoped), persisting to a path-jailed, size-capped per-widget file under `<stateDir>/dashboard/state/<widgetId>.json` — atomic writes, kept *separate* from `workspace.json` (does not count against the 256 KB workspace cap).\n- New bridge inbound messages `dashboard:setState` / `getState`, gated behind a new `state:persist` manifest capability (mirrors the existing `sendPrompt` gate).\n- The trusted parent resolves the widget's own `widgetId` — a widget can never read or write another widget's state, and a widget-supplied id is ignored.\n- Unit tests covering the store round-trip (persist → read-back), the 64 KB size-cap whole-reject, widget-id charset/traversal rejects, the capability gate, read/write scope, and state-vs-workspace separation — the `extensions/dashboard` suite (85 tests) and the UI dashboard suite (94 tests) are green.\n- This PR is the capability + its plumbing; the first shippable consumer is the stateful notes/todo widget (#101146), which depends on it.\n\n## How it works\nThe design mirrors the read path from #101098: **the widget never holds a credential and never talks to the gateway** — the trusted Control-UI parent brokers everything. On `dashboard:setState`, the parent calls `dashboard.widget.state.set` with the `widgetId` *it* already tracks for that iframe (`widget.id`); the widget's message carries only the opaque blob, and the `setWidgetState` bridge dependency takes *only* the blob — there is no code path by which a widget names another widget's state. State is capped at **64 KB** per widget (the serialized envelope, rejected whole *before* any write), stored under `<stateDir>/dashboard/state/<widgetId>.json` (`0o700` dir / `0o600` file), serialized through the store's process mutex and written atomically via `replaceFileAtomic`. The widget id is charset-guarded (`^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,48}$`) and the resolved path is re-checked for containment. The new `plugin.dashboard.widget-state.changed` broadcast carries `{ widgetId, version }` only — never the blob.\n\n## Security\nThis widens the trust surface, so it carries the same adversarial-review discipline as #101098. Verified in code and tests:\n- **(a) Own-state only** — the `widgetId` is always `widget.id`, bound by the trusted parent; the `setWidgetState` bridge dependency takes only the blob, and any id in the child's message is ignored.\n- **(b) Size cap** — 64 KB enforced on the serialized envelope *before* any write; oversize is rejected whole (nothing written).\n- **(c) Path jail** — the id is charset-guarded (`^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,48}$`) and the resolved `state/<widgetId>.json` path is re-checked for containment.\n- **(d) Capability gate** — `state:persist` is required; an ungated widget is denied *without touching the gateway*, the same shape as `sendPrompt`.\n- **(e) No new iframe reach** — the iframe still cannot reach the gateway; the parent holds the socket and calls the new RPCs on the widget's behalf.\n- **(f) Sandbox unchanged** — opaque origin, CSP `connect-src 'none'`, and the window-identity accept filter are all untouched.\n\nNote: this PR adds **no new dependency** — `pnpm-lock.yaml` is unchanged, so the dependency-graph guard should not trip.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n**Behavior or issue addressed:** Sandboxed custom widgets cannot persist their own state (the bridge is read-only), so any agent- or user-built interactive widget resets on reload. This adds a jailed, size-capped, capability-gated `setState`/`getState` path so a widget can save and restore its own state.\n**Evidence:** `node scripts/test-projects.mjs extensions/dashboard` → 85 passed (store persist/read-back round-trip, 64 KB whole-reject, widget-id charset/traversal rejects, capability gate, read/write scope, and proof that widget state is written under `state/<widgetId>.json` and never into `workspace.json`); `pnpm vitest run src/lib/dashboard` → 94 passed (bridge routes `setState`/`getState` only when the `state:persist` capability is present, and ignores any widget-supplied id); `pnpm ui:build` and oxlint clean.\n\n",
